{**
 * c-accordion - a column of c-collapse drawn as one block.
 *
 * The items are c-collapse and nothing else, the way c-signpost is made of
 * c-card: an item is a disclosure with a title and whatever it folds away, and
 * c-collapse already is one. So this block is only the frame, and the items go
 * in its accordionItems block:
 *
 *     {embed block accordion}
 *         {block accordionItems}
 *             {embed block collapse, title: 'First', level: 2, name: 'questions'}
 *                 {block collapseBody}...{/block}
 *             {/embed}
 *             ...
 *         {/block}
 *     {/embed}
 *
 * **One open at a time or any number open is one attribute, and it is the
 * browser's.** Items that share a name are opened one at a time - opening one
 * closes the others - with no script; items without a name open and close each
 * on its own. A browser too old to know a shared name opens any number, which
 * is the other variant and not a broken one.
 *
 * The level of the titles is the caller's too, because only the caller knows
 * where in the outline of the page the group lies.
 *}

{define accordion, ?string $testId = null}
    <div class="c-accordion" data-testid="{$testId}">{block accordionItems}{/block}</div>
{/define}
